# Native Android Standards & MVVM Clean Architecture

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep source, configuration, and verification evidence within approved systems. Use synthetic data in examples and redact credentials, private service details, and personal information from screenshots and logs.

Build screens from explicit state. Keep business rules independent of Android UI APIs. Give every asynchronous operation a clear owner, and keep persistence and networking behind repository contracts.

This guide defines the Android reference architecture and demonstrates a user profile: **read cached content, refresh remotely, persist a valid response, and publish the saved result**.

<Aside type="tip" title="Platform standard">
Use feature-oriented Clean Architecture and unidirectional data flow. Compose renders state and emits actions. A ViewModel coordinates use cases and exposes read-only StateFlow. Repositories implement domain contracts and own data access. The UI never calls Retrofit or Room directly.
</Aside>

