Follow the supplied single-responsibility file convention: give each class/interface its own dedicated file. Small declarations are grouped in some blocks below to show their relationship; split them into matching declaration-named files in the indicated package when integrating. Packages organize code, while separate Gradle modules and dependency rules enforce build-time boundaries. For a modular build, presentation and data depend on domain; the application composition root wires implementations.

