### Cached content, then refresh

<MermaidZoom title="Profile lifecycle · cache, refresh, and cancellation">

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UI as Compose lifecycle coroutine
    participant VM as ViewModel
    participant R as Use case / Repository
    participant DB as Room
    participant API as Authenticated API

    UI->>VM: Await load(accountId, userId)
    VM->>VM: Validate key, start request generation
    VM->>R: Read cached profile
    R->>R: Verify active account
    R->>DB: Read by account ID and user ID
    DB-->>VM: Domain snapshot through repository
    Note over VM: Render cached content if present
    VM->>R: Refresh profile
    R->>API: Request profile
    alt Valid response and successful write
        API-->>R: DTO with matching user ID
        R->>R: Check cancellation and active account
        R->>DB: Upsert account-scoped entity
        DB-->>R: Write completed
        R-->>VM: Saved domain snapshot
        VM-->>UI: Updated StateFlow
    else Recoverable refresh failure
        R-->>VM: Throw failure
        VM-->>UI: Keep cached content, show retry message
    else Expired session, denied access, or missing profile
        R->>DB: Delete this cached profile
        R-->>VM: Throw access or cleanup failure
        VM-->>UI: Clear displayed content, show safe message
    end
    Note over UI,VM: Stop, navigation, or changed effect keys cancel the load coroutine
    Note over VM,R: Cancellation checks and generation guards reject obsolete updates
```

</MermaidZoom>

**This is a snapshot-based reference, matching the iOS and React Native examples.** Successful refresh returns a value only after its Room write succeeds. It does not continuously observe database changes from other writers. If live updates are required, add a repository `Flow`, collect it with explicit ownership, and keep refresh status separate. Room supports both one-shot suspend reads and observable queries; do not describe one as the other. See [Room asynchronous queries](https://developer.android.com/training/data-storage/room/async-queries).

