### `core/profile/ProfileInfrastructure.kt`

These interfaces describe the integration the host application must provide; they do not assume an undocumented enterprise SDK API.

```kotlin
package com.enterprise.mobile.core.profile

import com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.domain.ProfileFailure
import javax.inject.Qualifier

@Qualifier
@Retention(AnnotationRetention.BINARY)
annotation class IoDispatcher

@Qualifier
@Retention(AnnotationRetention.BINARY)
annotation class MainDispatcher

fun interface EpochClock {
    fun nowMillis(): Long
}

interface ProfileSessionGuard {
    // Thread-safe, non-blocking; throw SESSION_EXPIRED or ACCESS_DENIED when invalid.
    fun requireActiveAccount(accountId: String)
}

interface ProfileDiagnostics {
    // Non-blocking and non-throwing. No credentials, IDs, payloads, or raw exceptions.
    fun report(stage: String, failure: ProfileFailure)
}
```

In a multi-module project, place reusable contracts in a dependency direction that does not make generic core infrastructure depend on a feature. Here, `core/profile` is a profile integration contract within the same target; it is not a proposed independent core Gradle module.

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · access checks complement session ownership">
The authenticated HTTP adapter must bind each request to the intended session. A guard around a mutable global client does not atomically capture credentials. The app must prevent an old account request from being executed with a new account's credentials, cancel old-session work, and replace protected navigation state. The guard is an additional check, not the authentication implementation.
</Aside>

