Errors are categories, not raw exception strings. Compose maps them to localized resources. Keeping content and refresh progress separate preserves useful cached data during a transient failure.

### `feature/user/presentation/UserProfileViewModel.kt`

```kotlin
package com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.presentation

import androidx.lifecycle.ViewModel
import com.enterprise.mobile.core.profile.MainDispatcher
import com.enterprise.mobile.core.profile.ProfileDiagnostics
import com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.domain.GetUserProfileUseCase
import com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.domain.ProfileException
import com.enterprise.mobile.feature.user.domain.ProfileFailure
import dagger.hilt.android.lifecycle.HiltViewModel
import javax.inject.Inject
import kotlinx.coroutines.CancellationException
import kotlinx.coroutines.CoroutineDispatcher
import kotlinx.coroutines.currentCoroutineContext
import kotlinx.coroutines.ensureActive
import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.MutableStateFlow
import kotlinx.coroutines.flow.asStateFlow
import kotlinx.coroutines.withContext

@HiltViewModel
class UserProfileViewModel @Inject constructor(
    private val profiles: GetUserProfileUseCase,
    private val diagnostics: ProfileDiagnostics,
    @MainDispatcher private val mainDispatcher: CoroutineDispatcher,
) : ViewModel() {
    private val mutableState = MutableStateFlow(UserProfileUiState())
    val state = mutableState.asStateFlow()
    private var generation = 0L

    // The route awaits this call. No nested unstructured coroutine is created.
    suspend fun load(accountId: String, userId: String) = withContext(mainDispatcher) {
        val request = ++generation
        val key = try {
            profiles.validatedKey(accountId, userId)
        } catch (_: ProfileException) {
            mutableState.value = UserProfileUiState(failure = ProfileFailure.INVALID_KEY)
            return@withContext
        }
        val previous = mutableState.value.takeIf { it.key == key } ?: UserProfileUiState(key = key)
        mutableState.value = previous.copy(isRefreshing = true, failure = null)
        try {
            try {
                val cached = profiles.cachedProfile(key)
                currentCoroutineContext().ensureActive()
                if (generation != request) return@withContext
                mutableState.value = mutableState.value.copy(user = cached)
            } catch (cancelled: CancellationException) {
                throw cancelled
            } catch (error: Exception) {
                currentCoroutineContext().ensureActive()
                if (generation != request) return@withContext
                val failure = category(error)
                if (failure in ACCESS_FAILURES) throw error
                diagnostics.report("cache-read", failure)
                // A recoverable cache-read failure must not block remote refresh.
            }
            val fresh = profiles.refreshProfile(key)
            currentCoroutineContext().ensureActive()
            if (generation != request) return@withContext
            mutableState.value = UserProfileUiState(key = key, user = fresh)
        } catch (cancelled: CancellationException) {
            throw cancelled
        } catch (error: Exception) {
            currentCoroutineContext().ensureActive()
            if (generation != request) return@withContext
            val failure = category(error)
            diagnostics.report("load", failure)
            mutableState.value = mutableState.value.copy(
                user = if (failure in ACCESS_FAILURES) null else mutableState.value.user,
                failure = failure,
            )
        } finally {
            if (generation == request) {
                mutableState.value = mutableState.value.copy(isRefreshing = false)
            }
        }
    }

    private fun category(error: Exception): ProfileFailure =
        (error as? ProfileException)?.failure ?: ProfileFailure.UNEXPECTED

    private companion object {
        val ACCESS_FAILURES = setOf(
            ProfileFailure.SESSION_EXPIRED,
            ProfileFailure.ACCESS_DENIED,
            ProfileFailure.NOT_FOUND,
            ProfileFailure.CACHE_INVALIDATION,
        )
    }
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · choose one owner for screen loading">
This reference intentionally lets the route own a visibility-bound load while the ViewModel retains state. The load is awaited and cancellation propagates down the same coroutine chain. Use `viewModelScope` instead when work should survive the screen becoming inactive, and document that different lifetime. Do not launch a ViewModel job from a route effect and assume cancelling the effect cancels that independent job.
</Aside>

All state coordination runs on the injected main dispatcher. Each request gets a generation number. After suspension, a cancelled or superseded request cannot publish content, an error, or a loading reset over a newer request. Keep diagnostic reporting non-throwing and lightweight.

