## Expected behavior

| Scenario | Expected result |
| :--- | :--- |
| Empty cache; successful refresh | Initial progress followed by the saved profile. |
| Cached profile; refresh running | Existing content stays visible with progress. |
| Cached profile; transient refresh failure | Retain content and display a safe retry message. |
| Cache read fails; refresh succeeds | Attempt remote recovery; show the successfully persisted profile. |
| Valid response; Room write fails | Refresh fails; do not display network-only data as a persisted success. |
| Missing body, malformed payload, or mismatched ID | Reject the response before persistence. |
| Session expired, access denied, or profile missing | Clear displayed content and invalidate this profile when handled by refresh; host completes access/session recovery. |
| Cache invalidation fails | Clear displayed content and surface an access-recovery category; host continues cleanup. |
| Account or profile changes | Clear other-profile content immediately and cancel the old effect. |
| Route becomes inactive | Cancel the screen-owned load; retain ViewModel state while its owner lives. |
| Route becomes active again | Start a new cache/read-refresh cycle under the lifecycle policy. |
| A dependency returns after cancellation | Cancellation/generation checks prevent stale UI updates. |
| Another writer changes Room | No automatic screen update in this snapshot example; add a real repository Flow if required. |

## Patterns to avoid

| Avoid | Use instead |
| :--- | :--- |
| Network or DAO calls inside composable bodies | Route effects through the ViewModel and use case. |
| Activity, View, or lifecycle-bound Context in a ViewModel | Inject focused application abstractions with appropriate ownership. |
| Public `MutableStateFlow` | Private writable state and a read-only `StateFlow` view. |
| Catching cancellation inside broad fallback logic | Rethrow `CancellationException` before handling other failures. |
| Raw exception messages in UI or logs | Typed failure categories, localized copy, and redacted diagnostics. |
| A full-screen spinner replacing cached content on every refresh | Independent content, progress, and failure properties. |
| Using `@Immutable` to silence stability concerns | Honor its contract and optimize based on measured rendering behavior. |
| Hardcoding dispatchers inside business/data operations | Inject dispatchers; configure their real implementations at the root. |
| Assuming a singleton is an account/session scope | Model session ownership and replacement explicitly. |
| Treating a cache or client-side flag as authorization | Enforce access on the backend and through the session coordinator. |

## Review checklist

- [ ] Feature boundaries match the domain/data/presentation structure; build rules enforce them where applicable.
- [ ] Domain code contains no Android framework, Compose, Room, or Retrofit imports.
- [ ] API contracts define required fields and expected statuses; identity is checked before persistence.
- [ ] Room reads, writes, and deletion use the account/profile composite key.
- [ ] Session guard and authenticated HTTP adapter agree on the intended account.
- [ ] Successful refresh requires a completed local write; failure remains explicit.
- [ ] Retry uses the current profile identity and keeps valid cached content visible.
- [ ] Coroutine cancellation propagates through route, ViewModel, use case, and data layer.
- [ ] Older requests cannot publish state or reset progress over a newer request.
- [ ] Error categories are mapped to localized resources, with appropriate recovery actions.
- [ ] Credentials and sensitive telemetry payloads are absent from UI state and profile storage.
- [ ] Hilt scopes and providers match the actual lifecycle; no duplicate infrastructure bindings exist.
- [ ] Database migration, backup, retention, and logout cleanup policies are covered.
- [ ] Accessibility, large text, offline launch, backgrounding, navigation, and account switching are exercised.
- [ ] Required CI gates and the defined 100% coverage scope and metrics pass.

