### Cached content, then refresh

<MermaidZoom title="Profile loading · success, failure, and cancellation">

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant V as SwiftUI task
    participant VM as Main-actor ViewModel
    participant R as Use case / Repository
    participant DB as SwiftData actor
    participant API as Remote source

    V->>VM: await load(userID)
    VM->>VM: Validate ID, start request generation
    VM->>R: Read account-scoped cache
    R->>DB: Read persistent record
    DB-->>VM: Domain snapshot through repository
    Note over VM: Display cached content if available
    VM->>R: Refresh profile
    R->>API: Fetch profile
    alt Valid response and successful save
        API-->>R: Validated DTO
        R->>DB: Update or insert, save
        DB-->>R: Saved domain snapshot
        R-->>VM: Refreshed profile
        VM-->>V: Updated observable state
    else Recoverable refresh failure
        R-->>VM: Throw failure
        VM-->>V: Retain cached content, show retry message
    else Access denied, expired session, or missing profile
        R->>DB: Invalidate this cached profile
        R-->>VM: Throw access or cleanup failure
        VM-->>V: Clear displayed profile, show safe message
    end
    Note over V,VM: View disappearance or task-ID change cancels the view task
    Note over VM,R: Cancellation checks and generation guard reject cancelled or obsolete results
```

</MermaidZoom>

**This is a snapshot-based read/refresh example, not a live database subscription.** Successful refresh returns the persisted snapshot. Changes made elsewhere do not automatically appear on this screen. If the product needs live updates, implement a real repository observation mechanism with defined ordering, buffering, cancellation, and subscriber cleanup. Do not return a one-value `AsyncStream` and call it continuous observation.

