### Repository.swift

The repository validates response identity, maps DTOs into domain values, and requires a successful save before returning a refreshed profile. A refresh failure remains a failure even when a cached record exists.

```swift
import Foundation

struct UserRepositoryImpl: UserRepository {
    private let accountID: String
    private let remote: any UserRemoteSource
    private let local: any UserLocalStore
    private let now: @Sendable () -> Date

    init(
        accountID: String,
        remote: any UserRemoteSource,
        local: any UserLocalStore,
        now: @escaping @Sendable () -> Date = { Date() }
    ) throws {
        guard !accountID.trimmingCharacters(in: .whitespacesAndNewlines).isEmpty else {
            throw UserProfileError.invalidConfiguration
        }
        self.accountID = accountID
        self.remote = remote
        self.local = local
        self.now = now
    }

    func cachedProfile(userID: String) async throws -> UserDomainModel? {
        try Task.checkCancellation()
        return try await local.read(accountID: accountID, userID: userID)
    }

    func refreshProfile(userID: String) async throws -> UserDomainModel {
        try Task.checkCancellation()
        let dto: UserNetworkDTO
        do {
            dto = try await remote.fetchProfile(userID: userID)
        } catch {
            if Task.isCancelled || error is CancellationError ||
                (error as? URLError)?.code == .cancelled {
                throw CancellationError()
            }
            if let failure = error as? UserProfileError,
               failure == .sessionExpired || failure == .accessDenied || failure == .notFound {
                // Invalidate this profile. Account-wide cleanup belongs to the session owner.
                do { try await local.remove(accountID: accountID, userID: userID) }
                catch {
                    if Task.isCancelled || error is CancellationError {
                        throw CancellationError()
                    }
                    throw UserProfileError.cacheInvalidationFailed
                }
            }
            throw error
        }
        try Task.checkCancellation()
        guard dto.id == userID else { throw UserProfileError.invalidPayload }
        let user = UserDomainModel(
            id: dto.id, name: dto.fullName, email: dto.email,
            isVIP: dto.isVIP, cachedAt: now()
        )
        // Never return network-only content as a successful persisted refresh.
        let saved = try await local.save(accountID: accountID, user: user)
        try Task.checkCancellation()
        return saved
    }
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · make time deterministic">
Inject `now` in tests. `cachedAt` records when this client prepared the cache update; it is not the server's last-modified timestamp and does not establish business freshness by itself. Add an explicit TTL or version policy if the product needs one.
</Aside>

This repository is a Sendable struct with immutable Sendable dependencies. The storage and remote actors isolate their mutable resources. It does not require `@unchecked Sendable`.

For access denial, session expiry, or a missing profile, this example invalidates the current cached record. A cleanup failure becomes a distinct error so the screen still clears its content. The session coordinator must independently block protected navigation and complete account-wide cleanup. A cache delete is not an authorization control.

Concurrent callers can still issue overlapping refreshes. The ViewModel's generation guard protects its screen, not global cache ordering. If multiple screens or background jobs refresh the same record, add a repository-level synchronization/version policy appropriate to the server contract; do not assume actor reentrancy or cancellation establishes “latest data wins.”

