### Required project tests

- [ ] Compile every reference file in the application's actual Swift configuration with concurrency checks enabled.
- [ ] Run SwiftData tests with an in-memory `ModelContainer`: insert, update, read, remove, account isolation, and uniqueness.
- [ ] Test migration and persistent-store initialization failures using the application's real schema.
- [ ] Exercise the real transport adapter with HTTP 200, 401, 403, 404, 5xx, empty/malformed payloads, timeouts, and cancellation.
- [ ] Verify refresh/retry uses the same current profile ID and handles cache-read failures.
- [ ] Verify account changes cancel work, replace route identity, and remove protected data.
- [ ] Verify no protected content appears after session revocation, including when cache cleanup fails.
- [ ] Check success, empty, initial loading, refresh loading, cached error, and fatal error layouts with accessibility tools.
- [ ] Test offline startup and foreground/background transitions on supported iOS versions.
- [ ] Meet the defined 100% coverage scope and metrics, and pass required CI gates.

## Production localization

The presentation example uses safe English messages to make the state transitions readable. Before shipping, map failures to localized resources or localized message keys, extract SwiftUI literals into the project’s String Catalog, and verify supported locales and Dynamic Type. Do not use raw server or system error descriptions as translated user copy.

## Common mistakes and corrections

| Mistake | Correct approach |
| :--- | :--- |
| Writing `Boolean` in Swift | Use `Bool`. |
| Marking a mutable repository `@unchecked Sendable` to silence diagnostics | Use compiler-checked immutable Sendable dependencies and isolate mutable resources. |
| Passing `ModelContext` or `@Model` instances across actors | Keep them inside the store actor; return Sendable domain snapshots. |
| Assuming an actor cannot interleave work across `await` | Account for reentrancy and define ordering for competing refreshes. |
| Starting a nested `Task` inside a view's `.task` and returning immediately | Await the load directly so view lifecycle cancellation reaches the operation. |
| Requiring `[weak self]` in every async closure | Analyze ownership and task lifetime. Weak capture alone does not cancel work or eliminate long-lived retention after `guard let self`. |
| Calling `ObservableObject` or `@Published` universally deprecated | Use Observation for this platform baseline; retain compatible legacy patterns where the application requires them. |
| Treating cached data as a successful refresh after any error | Preserve cached content and surface refresh failure separately. |
| Reporting raw technical errors in the UI | Map to safe localized messages and use redacted diagnostics. |
| Force-unwrapping configuration or crashing on store initialization | Validate configuration, propagate initialization errors, and provide recovery UI. |
| Describing all Keychain items as Secure Enclave protected | Use the approved Keychain abstraction; protection depends on item accessibility, key type, device, and configuration. |

