The persistent cache and Redux state have different jobs: MMKV retains validated snapshots across restarts; Redux owns the currently rendered state. This example does not subscribe to arbitrary MMKV changes or implement background synchronization. Add an explicit observation/synchronization policy if another writer must update the screen immediately.

## Reference implementation

The following files form one example. Keep their contracts together when adapting it. The host application supplies an authenticated HTTP adapter, managed encryption key, navigation focus, session lifecycle, localization, and design-system integration.

<Tabs>
  <TabItem label="1. Domain">

The domain contains no React, React Native, Redux, HTTP-client, or MMKV imports. `AbortSignal` is a cancellation contract provided by the runtime, not a Redux dependency.

### `src/features/user/domain/profile.ts`

```typescript
export interface UserDomainModel {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly name: string;
  readonly email: string;
  readonly isVip: boolean;
  readonly cachedAt: number;
}

export type ProfileErrorCode =
  | 'invalid-id' | 'cancelled' | 'unauthorized' | 'forbidden'
  | 'not-found' | 'http' | 'invalid-payload' | 'cache' | 'cache-invalidation';

export class ProfileError extends Error {
  constructor(readonly code: ProfileErrorCode) {
    super(`Profile operation failed: ${code}`);
    this.name = 'ProfileError';
  }
}

export function checkCancellation(signal: AbortSignal): void {
  if (signal.aborted) throw new ProfileError('cancelled');
}

export function isCancellation(error: unknown, signal: AbortSignal): boolean {
  return signal.aborted || (error instanceof ProfileError && error.code === 'cancelled');
}

/** One repository instance belongs to one authenticated account. */
export interface UserRepository {
  cachedProfile(userId: string): Promise<UserDomainModel | null>;
  refreshProfile(userId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<UserDomainModel>;
}

export class GetUserProfileUseCase {
  constructor(private readonly repository: UserRepository) {}

  normalizeId(rawId: string): string {
    const id = rawId.trim();
    // Example API contract; replace this rule if your API uses another ID format.
    if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$/.test(id)) throw new ProfileError('invalid-id');
    return id;
  }

  cachedProfile(userId: string): Promise<UserDomainModel | null> {
    return this.repository.cachedProfile(this.normalizeId(userId));
  }

  refreshProfile(userId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<UserDomainModel> {
    checkCancellation(signal);
    return this.repository.refreshProfile(this.normalizeId(userId), signal);
  }
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · types are not runtime validation">
`readonly` prevents reassignment during TypeScript checking; it does not freeze JavaScript objects. The data layer validates external values and freezes the flat domain snapshots it creates. Nested mutable objects would require a deliberate immutability policy. The sample ID format is an explicit API assumption—replace it if your real identifiers use a different format.
</Aside>

`cachedAt` is a client cache timestamp in milliseconds, not the server's modification time. Define freshness, expiry, and retention separately. See [TypeScript's readonly guidance](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/objects).

  </TabItem>
  <TabItem label="2. Remote boundary">

Inject the approved authenticated network client. The feature does not create a second Axios instance, hardcode an environment, or implement token refresh.

### `src/features/user/data/remote/userApiService.ts`

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';
import { checkCancellation, ProfileError } from '../../domain/profile';

// Required fields have no fabricated defaults. Match this schema to the API contract.
export const userNetworkSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().min(1),
  full_name: z.string().min(1),
  email: z.string(),
  is_vip: z.boolean(),
});
export type UserNetworkDTO = z.infer<typeof userNetworkSchema>;

/** Adapter contract implemented by the approved authenticated network SDK.
 * Resolve every HTTP response, including non-2xx. Reject transport errors.
 * Honor AbortSignal and normalize cancellation to ProfileError('cancelled').
 */
export interface ProfileHttpClient {
  getJson(path: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<{
    readonly status: number;
    readonly body: unknown;
  }>;
}

export interface UserRemoteSource {
  fetchProfile(userId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<UserNetworkDTO>;
}

export class UserApiService implements UserRemoteSource {
  constructor(private readonly http: ProfileHttpClient) {}

  async fetchProfile(userId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<UserNetworkDTO> {
    checkCancellation(signal);
    const response = await this.http.getJson(
      `/v1/users/${encodeURIComponent(userId)}`, signal,
    );
    checkCancellation(signal);
    switch (response.status) {
      case 200: break; // Endpoint contract requires a JSON profile body.
      case 401: throw new ProfileError('unauthorized');
      case 403: throw new ProfileError('forbidden');
      case 404: throw new ProfileError('not-found');
      default: throw new ProfileError('http');
    }
    const parsed = userNetworkSchema.safeParse(response.body);
    if (!parsed.success || parsed.data.id !== userId) {
      throw new ProfileError('invalid-payload');
    }
    return parsed.data;
  }
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · map HTTP failures deliberately">
The injected adapter must resolve HTTP responses—including non-2xx responses—into the stated contract, reject transport failures, and honor the abort signal. For an Axios-backed adapter, configure or map non-2xx handling explicitly. A 401 or 403 must not accidentally become an undifferentiated offline fallback.
</Aside>

The schema checks the response shape and requested identity. It does not prove authorization, email ownership, or business validity. Required fields have no invented defaults. Configure timeouts, response limits, redirects, and approved retry behavior in the shared network layer.

  </TabItem>
  <TabItem label="3. Local cache">

Cache records include a schema version, account ID, and domain snapshot. Cache reads validate both structure and identity; a type assertion after `JSON.parse` would provide no runtime protection.

### `src/features/user/data/local/userStorage.ts`

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';
import { ProfileError, type UserDomainModel } from '../../domain/profile';

/** Matches the string operations needed from an injected MMKV v4 instance.
 * The composition root owns instance creation, encryption keys, and teardown.
 */
export interface StringStorage {
  getString(key: string): string | undefined;
  set(key: string, value: string): void;
  remove(key: string): void;
}

export interface UserLocalStore {
  read(userId: string): UserDomainModel | null;
  save(user: UserDomainModel): UserDomainModel;
  remove(userId: string): void;
}

const cachedUserSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().min(1),
  name: z.string(),
  email: z.string(),
  isVip: z.boolean(),
  cachedAt: z.number().int().nonnegative(),
});
const envelopeSchema = z.object({
  schemaVersion: z.literal(1),
  accountId: z.string().min(1),
  user: cachedUserSchema,
});

export class UserStorage implements UserLocalStore {
  constructor(
    private readonly storage: StringStorage,
    private readonly accountId: string,
  ) {
    if (!accountId.trim()) throw new ProfileError('cache');
  }

  private key(userId: string): string {
    // JSON encoding prevents ambiguous account/user concatenation.
    return JSON.stringify(['user-profile', this.accountId, userId]);
  }

  read(userId: string): UserDomainModel | null {
    const key = this.key(userId);
    try {
      const raw = this.storage.getString(key);
      if (raw === undefined) return null;
      let decoded: unknown;
      try { decoded = JSON.parse(raw); }
      catch { this.storage.remove(key); return null; }
      const parsed = envelopeSchema.safeParse(decoded);
      if (!parsed.success || parsed.data.accountId !== this.accountId ||
          parsed.data.user.id !== userId) {
        this.storage.remove(key); // Disposable cache: discard incompatible records.
        return null;
      }
      return Object.freeze(parsed.data.user);
    } catch {
      throw new ProfileError('cache');
    }
  }

  save(user: UserDomainModel): UserDomainModel {
    try {
      const record = envelopeSchema.parse({
        schemaVersion: 1, accountId: this.accountId, user,
      });
      this.storage.set(this.key(user.id), JSON.stringify(record));
      return Object.freeze(record.user);
    } catch {
      throw new ProfileError('cache');
    }
  }

  remove(userId: string): void {
    try { this.storage.remove(this.key(userId)); }
    catch { throw new ProfileError('cache-invalidation'); }
  }
}
```

The sample treats the cache as disposable: malformed, incompatible, or incorrectly scoped records are removed and treated as absent. If deletion itself fails, the error propagates. For authoritative offline user edits, implement migrations and recovery rather than discarding records.

### `src/features/user/data/local/mmkvAdapter.ts`

```typescript
import { createMMKV } from 'react-native-mmkv';
import { ProfileError } from '../../domain/profile';
import type { StringStorage } from './userStorage';

/** Call once per account storage lifetime, after the secure key is available. */
export function createEncryptedProfileCache(
  instanceId: string,
  encryptionKey: string,
): StringStorage {
  if (!instanceId.trim() || !encryptionKey) throw new ProfileError('cache');
  return createMMKV({ id: instanceId, encryptionKey });
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · inject the key; never commit it">
Resolve the account cache key through the approved secure-storage/key-management integration before creating the MMKV instance. Pass an opaque instance namespace and a key valid for the installed MMKV version. Retain the instance for its owning account lifetime; do not construct it in a component body. Never use a fixed encryption key in source code or the JavaScript bundle.
</Aside>

MMKV encryption protects persisted cache data according to its configuration; it does not turn a profile cache into a credential vault. Keep authentication secrets in the approved native-backed auth SDK. Account namespacing prevents accidental cross-account reads, but does not replace logout cleanup or access control.

Synchronous native operations and JSON parsing still consume time on the calling JS thread. Keep records small and measure real workloads. Do not make universal latency or “times faster” guarantees from a library benchmark.

  </TabItem>
  <TabItem label="4. Repository and DI">

The repository maps a validated DTO, checks cancellation, and requires the local write to succeed before reporting refresh success. A cache-read API is separate from a refresh API, so an old cached profile cannot silently masquerade as a successful network refresh.

### `src/features/user/data/repository/userRepository.ts`

```typescript
import {
  checkCancellation, isCancellation, ProfileError,
  type UserDomainModel, type UserRepository,
} from '../../domain/profile';
import type { UserNetworkDTO, UserRemoteSource } from '../remote/userApiService';
import type { UserLocalStore } from '../local/userStorage';

export class UserRepositoryImpl implements UserRepository {
  constructor(
    private readonly remote: UserRemoteSource,
    private readonly local: UserLocalStore,
    private readonly now: () => number = Date.now,
  ) {}

  async cachedProfile(userId: string): Promise<UserDomainModel | null> {
    return this.local.read(userId);
  }

  async refreshProfile(userId: string, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<UserDomainModel> {
    checkCancellation(signal);
    let dto: UserNetworkDTO;
    try {
      dto = await this.remote.fetchProfile(userId, signal);
    } catch (error: unknown) {
      if (isCancellation(error, signal)) throw new ProfileError('cancelled');
      if (error instanceof ProfileError &&
          ['unauthorized', 'forbidden', 'not-found'].includes(error.code)) {
        this.local.remove(userId); // Cleanup failure must also reach the controller.
      }
      throw error;
    }
    checkCancellation(signal);
    if (dto.id !== userId) throw new ProfileError('invalid-payload');
    // The local adapter must succeed before refresh is reported as successful.
    return this.local.save(Object.freeze({
      id: dto.id, name: dto.full_name, email: dto.email,
      isVip: dto.is_vip, cachedAt: this.now(),
    }));
  }
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · cancellation must reach the write boundary">
Pass the same signal through the thunk, use case, repository, and remote adapter. Check it after the remote await and before the synchronous cache write. Cancelling a request does not undo a write that has already completed. Server-side work may also continue after client cancellation.
</Aside>

Unauthorized, forbidden, and missing-profile errors invalidate this profile's cached record. A failed removal propagates `cache-invalidation`, causing the screen to clear its content. The application session coordinator must independently block protected navigation and complete account-wide cleanup.

