## Expected behavior

| Scenario | Expected result |
| :--- | :--- |
| Empty cache; valid remote response | Show initial progress, then the saved profile. |
| Cached profile; refresh running | Keep content visible with a refresh indicator. |
| Cached profile; timeout or server failure | Retain content and show a retry message; do not report a successful refresh. |
| Cache JSON malformed or schema incompatible | Remove the disposable record and request fresh data. |
| Cache read fails | Report the failure category and attempt remote refresh. |
| Valid response; cache write fails | Reject refresh rather than claiming persisted success. |
| Response ID differs from requested ID | Reject the payload without writing it. |
| Session expires, access is denied, or profile is missing | Invalidate this record and clear displayed content; host handles access/session recovery. |
| Cache invalidation fails | Clear displayed content and report a recovery message; host continues cleanup. |
| A newer request starts | Abort the older screen request; request-ID guards reject late updates. |
| Two profile screens are mounted | Maintain separate screen entries and request IDs. |
| Screen loses activity or unmounts | Abort the screen request; remove its entry on unmount. |
| State is reset before an old request completes | The old completion cannot recreate a missing entry. |
| Another writer changes MMKV | No automatic screen update in this snapshot example. |

