# Enterprise App Foundations Suite

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep company source, assets, configuration, and verification evidence within approved systems. Use synthetic test data. Never include credentials, private delivery links, sensitive payloads, or personal data in examples, screenshots, logs, or AI prompts.

Build product features on shared foundations with clear ownership, predictable lifecycle behavior, and platform-appropriate implementations.

This guide covers six capabilities: **Design & Theming, Security & Credential Storage, Localization, Push Notifications, Branding, and Account Data Cleanup**. Each foundation defines its responsibilities, integration boundary, failure behavior, and implementation hints. React Native examples retain Redux Toolkit for shared preferences and application state.

<Aside type="tip" title="Platform standard">
Use approved foundation implementations and generated resources. Where a confirmed SDK owns a capability, integrate through its documented contract. Product features consume semantic tokens and typed service contracts; they do not create their own credential stores, notification routers, or account-wipe routines. Android, iOS, and React Native share behavioral requirements while using their own platform APIs.
</Aside>

