## Account Data Cleanup & Wipe Recovery

**Responsibility:** Make protected account data unavailable immediately, stop new writes, remove the resources the app owns, verify the result, and recover safely after interruption.

Use this foundation for logout, account removal, authorized offboarding, and validated device-policy actions. An incoming push or a local root/jailbreak signal is not automatically an authenticated wipe command; validate authority, target scope, replay protection, and policy before invoking destructive cleanup.

<Aside type="caution" title="Define an achievable guarantee">
App-level cleanup is not one atomic transaction across Keychain/Keystore, databases, files, caches, and Redux. File deletion does not guarantee physical overwriting on flash storage or removal from backups, shared services, server systems, or previously captured telemetry. Report a verified scoped cleanup outcome rather than promising “zero residual” or “100% shredding.”
</Aside>

### Recoverable cleanup lifecycle

