## Integration and review checklist

- [ ] Each foundation has an owner, typed contract, documented lifetime, and approved implementation.
- [ ] Design tokens are versioned/generated; semantic light/dark pairs and actual color combinations are reviewed.
- [ ] React Native shared preferences use Redux Toolkit; providers distribute derived values rather than owning duplicate preference state.
- [ ] Credentials use the approved native-backed adapter; no secrets or fixed encryption keys appear in source or Redux.
- [ ] Locked storage, key invalidation, biometric cancellation, and missing credentials are distinguished.
- [ ] Network trust/pinning configuration follows reviewed policy and a maintained rotation/recovery process.
- [ ] Localization uses supported tags, fallbacks, native resources, correct plurals, and explicit RTL/restart behavior.
- [ ] Push adapters cover registration changes, foreground/background/cold-start paths, permission denial, and subscription cleanup.
- [ ] Notification intents are validated, deduplicated, session-aware, and authorized before navigation.
- [ ] Branding publishes a coherent approved token/asset set and handles icon/platform failure without corrupting the in-app theme.
- [ ] Cleanup has a scoped resource inventory, writer barrier, durable checkpoint, failure reporting, and restart recovery.
- [ ] Account cleanup resets protected in-memory/Redux/navigation state and verifies the registered persistent resources.
- [ ] No guarantee depends on timely push delivery, a universal hardware vault, or atomic cross-storage deletion.
- [ ] Tests meet the defined 100% production coverage scope and metrics, with documented exclusions.
- [ ] Actual Android/iOS builds, platform resources, native SDK setup, accessibility, and required CI gates are verified.

